.\n\nThe battle rages on, and a depressed Shinji hides deep within NERV's headquarters. With the fate of the world resting in Shinji's hands, Captain Misato Katsuragi hunts for the teenage boy as society crumbles around them.\n\n(Source: MAL Rewrite)\n\nNote: Alternate version of the Shin Seiki Evangelion ending, which either supplements or replaces episodes 25 and 26, depending on how they are viewed."},"tags":[{"name":"Philosophy","rank":95,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Tragedy","rank":93,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Coming of Age","rank":89,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Post-Apocalyptic","rank":89,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Denpa","rank":89,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Dystopian","rank":87,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Meta","rank":87,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":82,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Gods","rank":82,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Psychosexual","rank":81,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Body Horror","rank":80,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Conspiracy","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Super Robot","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Gore","rank":78,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Primarily Teen Cast","rank":76,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Cosmic Horror","rank":76,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Afterlife","rank":74,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Kaiju","rank":71,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Mythology","rank":71,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Robots","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Religion","rank":69,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Female Protagonist","rank":64,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Mixed Media","rank":61,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Nudity","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Clone","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Masturbation","rank":56,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Guns","rank":55,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Rape","rank":55,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Tsundere","rank":52,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Angels","rank":50,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Politics","rank":49,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Space","rank":45,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Kuudere","rank":36,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Bisexual","rank":13,"spoiler":tr